0..61 Comment "// This source shows the machine widths and their operations."
62..64 Comment "//"
65..135 Comment "// `u8`, `u16`, `i8`, `i16`, `usize` and `isize` join the four widths."
136..197 Comment "// `usize` and `isize` hold 64 bits, the word of each target."
198..264 Comment "// Each width has the same forms, called by their qualified names."
265..267 Comment "//"
268..337 Comment "// A `wrapping_` form reduces its result modulo two to the bit count."
338..401 Comment "// A `saturating_` form clamps its result to the nearest bound."
402..473 Comment "// A `checked_` form answers `w + Unit`, with the absence on the right."
474..476 Comment "//"
477..550 Comment "// - see: Rust `u8::wrapping_add`, `u8::checked_add` — integer methods."
